  <static seed="2108" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionPercentDecimal/DecimalToFraction35.pg">
    <statement><p>Write the decimal number as a fraction.</p>
<p><m>4.35</m> = <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4{\textstyle\frac{7}{20}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The integer part of the decimal <m>4.35</m> will not change. We will only change the decimal part--0.35.</p>
<p><m>0.35</m> is read as thirty-five hundredth, so it can be written as <m>\frac{35}{100}</m>, which can be reduced to <m>{{\frac{7}{20}}}</m> by dividing <m>5</m> in both the numerator and denominator.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 4.35 = {4{\textstyle\frac{7}{20}}} }</m></p>
</solution>
